# ─── Supabase (the only variables the app actually requires) ─────────────────
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Service role key — server-side only, never exposed to the browser.
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# ─── Search engine verification (optional) ──────────────────────────────────
# Per-domain. Omit and the meta tag is simply not rendered, which is the right
# default — a wrong token is worse than none. For a Search Console *Domain*
# property use DNS TXT instead; these are for URL-prefix properties.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# ─── Extra admin accounts (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated, additive to ADMIN_EMAILS in src/lib/admin.ts.
# Only ever list addresses on a domain you control.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=

# ─── Deliberately NOT configurable ──────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL — do not set this. The canonical origin is hardcoded in
#   src/lib/site.ts. A stale value here once pointed the whole live site at a
#   suspended domain: every canonical, all JSON-LD, the robots.txt Host and all
#   2,300 sitemap URLs.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER — also hardcoded in src/lib/site.ts, so a stale
#   value cannot bring back a previous/banned number.
#
# Stripe is NOT used. Payment is manual: PayID + crypto with WhatsApp follow-up.
